From 2016d8e5d609acae471da214ae77e43a5ed18858 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 21:29:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] reaper_inject: never bounce first-run gate pages (fix
 factory-reset UI loop) [v1.5.0e]

A factory-reset RT-BE96U looped its web UI ('bricked, keeps going in circles') --
found and reported by tester PorscheT. Root cause: on a factory-clean box state.js
force-redirects the top window to a gate page until setup completes: Main_Password.asp
while the admin password is still default, QIS_wizard.htm while w_Setting=0 / sdn_rl
unconfigured. But reaper_inject.c's serve-time bounce rewrote those gate pages into
reaper_shell.asp, whose state.js redirected right back -- an infinite ping-pong with
no way to reach the password page to escape. Reaper's earlier QIS removal handled the
x_Setting/w_Setting path but not these gate redirects.

Fix (bounce side, one place, covers every state.js trigger): add Main_Password.asp and
QIS_wizard.htm to reaper_skip[], plus a QIS_* prefix skip in reaper_should_inject(), so
the gate pages stay top-level. Post-reset flow is now login -> forced password change ->
dashboard, no loop. Verified in mock_router.py. Bump v1.5.0e.

Reported-by: PorscheT
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 release/src-rt/version.conf              |  2 +-
 release/src/router/httpd/reaper_inject.c | 15 +++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 16 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/release/src-rt/version.conf b/release/src-rt/version.conf
index 598c6cff42..11ddeaf2b1 100644
--- a/release/src-rt/version.conf
+++ b/release/src-rt/version.conf
@@ -4,6 +4,6 @@ KERNEL_VER_AM=$(subst .,,$(KERNEL_VER))
 FS_VER_AM=$(subst .,,$(FS_VER))
 
 SERIALNO=102.8
-EXTENDNO=Reaper_v1.5.0d
+EXTENDNO=Reaper_v1.5.0e
 
 RCNO=0
diff --git a/release/src/router/httpd/reaper_inject.c b/release/src/router/httpd/reaper_inject.c
index 69c5e6b086..f223b5c68f 100644
--- a/release/src/router/httpd/reaper_inject.c
+++ b/release/src/router/httpd/reaper_inject.c
@@ -80,6 +80,16 @@ static const char *reaper_skip[] = {
 	"Reaper_Traffic.asp",
 	"Main_Login.asp",
 	"Nologin.asp",
+	/* First-run GATE pages: on a factory-clean box state.js force-redirects the
+	   TOP window to these until setup is complete -- Main_Password.asp while the
+	   admin password is still default, QIS_wizard.htm while w_Setting=0 / sdn_rl
+	   is unconfigured. If the bounce rewrites them into reaper_shell.asp, state.js
+	   redirects straight back and it loops forever (a factory reset "bricks" the
+	   UI, and the password page can never be reached to escape). Keep the gate
+	   pages TOP-LEVEL so the user can finish setup. (All QIS_* pages are also
+	   matched by the prefix check in reaper_should_inject().) */
+	"Main_Password.asp",
+	"QIS_wizard.htm",
 	/* Captive_Portal* embed a </head> INSIDE a <script> splash template before
 	   the real </head>; injecting at the first </head> would land inside the
 	   script and prematurely close it. They are the only multi-</head> pages, so
@@ -156,6 +166,11 @@ static int reaper_should_inject(struct mime_handler *h, const char *file)
 		if (strcasecmp(name, reaper_skip[i]) == 0)
 			return 0;
 
+	/* Any QIS_* setup page is a first-run gate page (see reaper_skip[]): never
+	   bounce it, or the setup wizard loops on a factory-clean box. */
+	if (strncasecmp(name, "QIS_", 4) == 0)
+		return 0;
+
 	return 1;
 }
 
